Use case: stylized-concept. Production IN-GAME ACTION sprite atlas, exactly EIGHT cells, FOUR columns TWO rows with equal cell dimensions, transparent background. Reference image is IDENTITY and illustration style reference for SOL, preserve exactly their outfit, helmet, body, braid if present, shoes, gloves, board and wheel colors. Draw the same character RACING on a downhill longboard, seen from BEHIND from chase camera about 1.5m high, very slightly looking down. Realistic anatomy, premium crisp painterly pixel art arcade sprites matching reference; never a glossy 3D render. This is NOT the selection turnaround; all first six frames are rear racing views from same camera.
Top row left to right:
1 neutral riding stance facing away, bent knees moderately crouched, both feet firmly on board;
2 carving left, body leaning left, LEFT arm tucked inward left of body, both hands above ground, board turns slightly left;
3 carving right, body leaning right, RIGHT arm inside right, hands above ground, board turns slightly right;
4 hard LEFT slide, torso low, LEFT gloved palm contacting asphalt on screen left, board yawed diagonally and skidding, knees bent.
Bottom row left to right:
5 hard RIGHT slide, RIGHT gloved palm touching ground on screen right, torso low, board yawed opposite left slide;
6 deep aerodynamic tuck, compact crouch, chest on forward thigh, both arms held behind lower back, feet still on board;
7 beginning a fall, rider tumbling SIDEWAYS at low height, feet separated from longboard, no board in this cell;
8 rider on their side sliding along the ground, helmet and gloves visible, limbs anatomically natural, no board in this cell.
Full figure contained inside every cell, consistent character scale, empty transparent margins, exact 4x2 layout and no labels. Detailed cloth folds, readable dark silhouettes, warm sunset rim light, limited clustered colors, clean hard pixel edges. No smoke, no trails, NO background, NO ground plane, NO cast shadow, NO grid lines, no text. The atlas will be cropped into animated sprites by game engine. Output landscape 1536x1024 or larger.

